    {
      "chunkId": "hrp-fitness-0002",
      "sourceId": "hrp-fitness",
      "sectionOrPage": "What can be done about it?",
      "text": "Six to seven days a week, astronauts on the International Space Station perform resistance training and aerobic exercises for 1.5 hours per day to maintain their fitness and protect against muscle and bone loss. Crew members also undergo periodic fitness self-evaluations to help researchers monitor their health and fitness and to optimize the astronauts’ training regimen. Spacecraft set to carry astronauts to the Moon and Mars, however, will likely have less space for exercise equipment. Consequently, researchers are working to understand how to optimize both exercise machines and protocols to ensure that astronaut health is maintained on these deep space missions.",
